@@ -641,6 +641,30 @@ The host provides:
 
 The worker executes the tool and returns a typed result (string content, structured data, or error).
 
+### 13.11 `resolveRunModel`
+
+Decides the model for one issue run before the run starts. Requires the `run.model.resolve` capability. Only one plugin per company may hold this capability.
+
+The host calls this method inside run execution, after it reads the issue override and before it merges the adapter config. The host provides:
+
+- run ID, company ID, agent ID, issue ID, adapter type, invocation source and wake reason
+- the agent default model
+- the previous run on the same issue and agent, with its decision ID
+- the issue override model, if any
+- the deadline in milliseconds
+
+The worker returns one of three answers:
+
+- `decide`: run on `model`. The answer can also set `effort` and `env`. Every `env` key must be declared in the manifest field `modelRouting.envKeys`. Values must be plain strings. The host rejects a key that is a secret binding in the agent config.
+- `keep`: the agent default or the existing override is correct.
+- `defer`: no decision yet. The host parks the run and retries later.
+
+The decision applies to this run only. The host records it in the run context as `modelDecision`.
+
+The host skips the call for runs without an issue, issues assigned to a human, and issues that carry an override model.
+
+The instance setting `requireRunModelDecision` is off by default. While it is off, the call is advisory: the host records the answer and the run starts on the configured model. While it is on, an invalid answer, a timeout or `defer` parks the run as a bounded retry. After the last retry the host surfaces the issue. The run never starts on the default model. A run that a user requested directly is exempt and starts on the default model.
+
 ## 14. SDK Surface
 
 Plugins do not talk to the DB directly.
